      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2023-june/q1",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:110mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9fm0-02-2023-june/q01-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. A shaded region R above the initial line, bounded by a curve that starts at the pole O on the initial line and sweeps anticlockwise to the line theta = pi on the left.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows a sketch of the curve with polar equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=2\\sqrt{\\sinh\\theta+\\cosh\\theta}\\qquad0\\leqslant\\theta\\leqslant\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>, shown shaded in Figure 1, is bounded by the initial line, the curve and the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\pi\"></span></p><p>Use algebraic integration to determine the exact area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\\mathrm e^q-r\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> are real numbers to be found.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p>",
