      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2023-june/q4",
      "question": "<ol class=\"parts\"><li>Sketch the polar curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span>, with equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=3+\\sqrt5\\cos\\theta\\qquad0\\leqslant\\theta\\leqslant2\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>On your sketch clearly label the pole, the initial line and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> at the point where the curve intersects the initial line.</p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The tangent to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;\\theta&lt;\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\"></span>, is parallel to the initial line.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Use calculus to show that at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt5}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li><li>Hence determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
