      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2023-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>The points representing the complex numbers <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_1=35-25\\mathrm i\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z_2=-29+39\\mathrm i\"></span> are opposite vertices of a regular hexagon, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span>, in the complex plane.</p><p>The centre of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> represents the complex number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=3+7\\mathrm i\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta=\\dfrac{1+\\mathrm i}{64}\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\beta\\left(z_1-\\alpha\\right)=1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span> are given by the roots of the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left(\\beta(z-\\alpha)\\right)^6=1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>Write down the roots of the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"w^6=1\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\\mathrm e^{\\mathrm i\\theta}\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Hence, or otherwise, determine the position of the other four vertices of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\"></span>, giving your answers as complex numbers in Cartesian form. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
