    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9fm0-02-2023-june/q8",
      "question": "<p>Given that a cubic equation has three distinct roots that all lie on the same straight line in the complex plane,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>describe the possible lines the roots can lie on. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=8z^3+bz^2+cz+d\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d\"></span> are real constants.</p><p>The roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)\"></span> are distinct and lie on a straight line in the complex plane.</p><p>Given that one of the roots is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{3}{2}+\\dfrac{3}{2}\\mathrm i\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>state the other two roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(z)=z^3+Pz^2+Qz+12\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> are real constants, has 3 distinct roots.</p><p>The roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(z)\"></span> lie on a different straight line in the complex plane than the roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)\"></span></p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(z)\"></span> have one root in common</li><li>one of the roots of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(z)\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-4\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>write down the value of the common root, <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>determine the value of the other root of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm g(z)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol></li><li>Hence solve the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(z)=\\mathrm g(z)\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
