      "question": "<p>A patient is treated by administering an antibiotic intravenously at a constant rate for some time.</p><p>Initially there is none of the antibiotic in the patient.</p><p>At time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after treatment began</p><ul><li>the concentration of the antibiotic in the blood of the patient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\,\\mathrm{mg/ml}\"></span></li><li>the concentration of the antibiotic in the tissue of the patient is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\\,\\mathrm{mg/ml}\"></span></li></ul><p>The concentration of antibiotic in the patient is modelled by the equations</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dx}{\\mathrm dt}=0.025y-0.045x+2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}=0.032x-0.025y\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"40\\,000\\frac{\\mathrm d^2y}{\\mathrm dt^2}+2800\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dt}+13y=2560\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Determine, according to the model, a general solution for the concentration of the antibiotic in the patient’s tissue at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after treatment began. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence determine a particular solution for the concentration of the antibiotic in the tissue at time <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> minutes after treatment began. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>To be effective for the patient the concentration of antibiotic in the tissue must eventually reach a level between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"185\\,\\mathrm{mg/ml}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"200\\,\\mathrm{mg/ml}\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>Determine whether the rate of administration of the antibiotic is effective for the patient, giving a reason for your answer. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
